{{- /*
Shared Homebrew PATH snippet — included by every shell init file and every
run_once script that needs `brew` (dotfiles#7).

Homebrew's installer never writes its own PATH line anywhere; it only *prints*
an `eval "$(... brew shellenv)"` for the user to copy-paste. In an automated
chezmoi apply nobody reads that output, so brew ends up installed but invisible
to every shell. This snippet is the single place that knows where brew can
live, so the shells, the install scripts, and the CI assertions can't drift
apart.

POSIX sh only — it is sourced from sh, bash and zsh.

Prefixes, in priority order:
  darwin: /opt/homebrew  (Apple Silicon — the only prefix the installer
                          supports today)
          /usr/local     (Intel, pre-existing installs)
  linux:  /home/linuxbrew/.linuxbrew  (default; installer had root or sudo)
          $HOME/.linuxbrew            (per-user prefix via HOMEBREW_PREFIX)

Silent no-op when none of them exist — on Alpine/musl there is no Homebrew at
all and core tools come from apk (#62).
*/ -}}
for __brew in {{ if eq .chezmoi.os "darwin" }}/opt/homebrew/bin/brew /usr/local/bin/brew{{ else }}/home/linuxbrew/.linuxbrew/bin/brew "$HOME/.linuxbrew/bin/brew"{{ end }}; do
  if [ -x "$__brew" ]; then
    eval "$("$__brew" shellenv)"
    break
  fi
done
unset __brew
